  "text": "# bko-holt load plan for layout.json\n# Source: ?, Redox, BIOS boot with redox, dumped 2026-11-08T02:53:51Z\n#\n# Disks:\n#   vdb (16 GiB) -> /dev/sdq\n#\n# Notes:\n#   - vdb2: the ESP, written as the source's with the partition table\n\n# ---- partition ----\n# vdb -> /dev/sdq: clear the old table and signatures\nwipefs --all /dev/sdq\n# vdb -> /dev/sdq: the source's table, GUIDs and boot code exactly\nsh -c 'bko-holt write-table layout.json vdb /dev/sdq $(blockdev --getsize64 /dev/sdq)'\n# the kernel reads the new table\npartx -u /dev/sdq\nudevadm settle\n\n# ---- assemble ----\n# (nothing to do)\n\n# ---- format ----\n# vdb3: RedoxFS\nredoxfs-mkfs /dev/sdq3\n# vdb4: swap \"swap\"\nmkswap -U bc000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007 -L swap --pagesize 4096 /dev/sdq4\n# check: /dev/sdq4 is swap with the source's UUID, label and page size (read back by bko-holt's own probe)\n\n# ---- mount ----\nmkdir -p /mnt/bko-target\nsh -c 'redoxfs /dev/sdq3 /mnt/bko-target >/run/bko-holt/redoxfs.log 2>&1 </dev/null; i=0; until mountpoint -q /mnt/bko-target; do i=$((i + 1)); [ $i -lt 60 ] || { cat /run/bko-holt/redoxfs.log; exit 1; }; sleep 1; done'\n\n# ---- restore ----\n# snapshot latest of /srv/bko-repo, with BackOtter's restore flags\nRUSTIC_STRICT_EXIT=true rustic-bko --repository /srv/bko-repo --no-progress restore --numeric-id latest /mnt/bko-target\n\n# ---- boot ----\n# the boot code (MBR, freebsd-boot) was written with the partition table\nmkdir -p /mnt/bko-target/var/log/bko-holt\n# this restore's log, on the restored system\ncp -Rp /run/bko-holt/log/. /mnt/bko-target/var/log/bko-holt/\n\n# ---- close ----\n# the restored tree\numount --recursive /mnt/bko-target\n\n# Nothing was written.  To run it: bko-holt load layout.json ... --through close --commit\n"
